 - Only 19% of homes match a sale, so 81% of current values are model estimates. Most past sales have no known rating at sale, because the EPC extract covers 2025–26 only.
 - Relevance labels from EPC recommendations are rule-based, computed from the same fields we use as features.
 - Condensing-boiler status is inferred from the EPC efficiency rating, and almost all gas boilers are rated Good, so the boiler upgrade is rarely feasible.
+
+
+## Optional thermostat signal (`setpoint_reported_c`)
+
+A noisy, partial report of the home's usual heating temperature, as a household or a smart thermostat could supply. **Simulated.**
+
+- Generated in `gen/telemetry.py`: hidden setpoint + N(0, 0.7 C), rounded to 0.5 C, clipped to 14-26 C, for a random 30% of homes; NaN for the rest (never zero).
+- It is an input only. No label is derived from it, and `hidden/` is still never a feature source.
+- It uses its own random stream (seed, 20261011), so every other output of a seeded build is unchanged.
+- It makes the thermostat-driven part of the retrofit savings (smart controls, and part of wall insulation) partly predictable. **Any accuracy gain from it is a property of the simulator's design, not evidence about real homes; report results with and without it.**
+- Checks: `validate.py` section 7 (coverage, noise level, plausible range).
